	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nuN5YS0BHq576KC6j",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 5, DX 8, IQ 10, HT 10, HP 5, WILL 12, PER 11, FP 10, SPEED 4.5, MOVE 2, DODGE 7, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nATL3PI3RmCE30xx_",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 1 (offense -8, protection -5), threat tier minor, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nfxBP0D-hXIJa8oDz",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/awakened-shrub.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nQUEoLgtJ0SCavIqs",
			"text": "Independent build total: 0 points of racial traits plus 1 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "nMepzzvKoNp6LRWP5",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Awakened Shrub (SRD 5.1). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nfFk-eqSofdf61cwx",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nSMgRO1-rjeE3A6Qa",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 20 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "nL07bTXKg8QdISObm",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 2 (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "n_YGyzCdPWxJi27Ox",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "nuaAXeSe1_irud4NT",
			"text": "About a metre across, which is the SM -2 row."
		},
		{
			"id": "nsjelEdqIKMQ6o7G2",
			"text": "IQ 10 and no Cannot Speak: an awakened plant is awake in the full sense and holds a conversation, which is the whole reason a GM puts one in a scene."
		},
		{
			"id": "nrhlYdQudQadci_Fb",
			"text": "Fire is the obvious answer to it and the build does not pretend otherwise. Vulnerability is not modelled as a trait here because the package has no vulnerability contract yet; a GM should simply rule it."
		},
		{
			"id": "noiRgI5AdyCO3JcH-",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
